            <ArticleTitle>[A young woman with acute abdominal pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A5496</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 17-year-old woman was operated in a Tanzanian hospital because of a suspected ruptured ectopic pregnancy. During laparatomy an interstitial ectopic pregnancy with an intact gestational sac was found. The ectopic pregnancy had ruptured into the abdominal cavity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
